{"event_type":"review","id":"6afca5f5815deadf56861c07a3f02479c134b180b6ee90d8a76973ead24cdf10","occurred_at":"2026-11-08T15:05:34Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/61ba19995e13cb170a97636356c2b6c1e5272a24c2245e1d4181be3f55b259a7","sha256":"61ba19995e13cb170a97636356c2b6c1e5272a24c2245e1d4181be3f55b259a7"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/b89a246bb83d921e86084b32c1f48f1325109ef604f1684d8c2b24a6bf36cf5b","sha256":"b89a246bb83d921e86084b32c1f48f1325109ef604f1684d8c2b24a6bf36cf5b"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/92e6c0afb86a254b3da3935db97e64beabb39af7ea9e463ffc7d5f1225b38096","sha256":"92e6c0afb86a254b3da3935db97e64beabb39af7ea9e463ffc7d5f1225b38096"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/3b73f1517abb75e0341578e3da4936dcb243fa9eae6221ee225123f5e4006e4d","sha256":"3b73f1517abb75e0341578e3da4936dcb243fa9eae6221ee225123f5e4006e4d"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/732a0a13aff44fa8d0da98b75de6b1eadab53ff4afae231caa5fed194e4e9731","sha256":"732a0a13aff44fa8d0da98b75de6b1eadab53ff4afae231caa5fed194e4e9731"}],"attempt_id":"c199a92a258664412fab770657466206fa65833b652e6a1f003bb84ee7ac2e4f:0:1","base":"e263f66c059271fe89ea4b93f23fdd0c0815c512","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"e5bf59fd9a26d375c91b58cffd5f7944b9c22d35","body":"**Pass `PATH` (and `HOME`) to the `git` child, or resolve a trusted binary.**\n\n`env` at Lines 24-29 replaces the whole process environment. Without `PATH`, Node looks up `git` only in the execvp default search path (`/usr/bin:/bin`). On hosts where git is elsewhere (Nix, a custom toolchain path), `execFile` fails with ENOENT. After that, `headMessage` reports HEAD as unavailable and `evidenceRoot` throws.\n\n`GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null` also drops a globally configured `safe.directory`. In container CI with a checkout owned by another user, git then refuses with \"dubious ownership\". Forward `PATH: processEnv().PATH`, or reuse the trusted-binary resolution in addressEvidence.ts Lines 229-245.","id":"49a4c9a7fd752a028688250ca5324e05ec16a9f81b07f36808b15e15f82e6f20","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/localReview.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Pass `PATH` (and `HOME`) to the `git` child, or resolve a trusted binary."},{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"f41687b38c35b5def763d935ec2b071ebba08574","body":"**Allow glob characters in foreign file names.**\n\nIn `addressEvidence.ts:797`, `terminalPath` rejects foreign tracked files such as `app/[slug]/page.tsx`, although this path is only read and hashed. If a touched worker is deferred on parent cancellation, this refusal can quarantine the owner and block later admissions until attended recovery.\n\nAllow these characters for foreign files while retaining the existing checks for attempted files.\n\n<details>\n<summary>Suggested fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-async function terminalPath(root: string, file: string) {\n+async function terminalPath(root: string, file: string, allowGlob = false) {\n@@\n-    /[*?\\[\\]{}]/.test(file)\n+    (!allowGlob && /[*?\\[\\]{}]/.test(file))\n@@\n-        const foreign = await terminalPath(attempt.root, file);\n+        const foreign = await terminalPath(attempt.root, file, true);\n```\n\n</details>","id":"2f9f8238fb43de382a3f03db7bd9e7c13441ac99d2b91ab2b13b21dc58bf8816","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts","severity":"major","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Allow glob characters in foreign file names."}],"head":"5bc914d24be1904765ea927b5eb2edeac503afe8","head_tree":"f3d13794b479ccd72ccb765c7289aa9698c4c59f","input_scope":[{"blob":"f41687b38c35b5def763d935ec2b071ebba08574","intervals":[[1,1012]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts"},{"blob":"adbac9f6189b09c3e3713da8052822e48ab5e227","intervals":[[1,38]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressFileIdentity.ts"},{"blob":"cdffef4988b23df03fcc18008e63409e025604b7","intervals":[[1,1122]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressOwnership.ts"},{"blob":"3ce4c1e2b433f255d96512bfac9ba5e745656a05","intervals":[[1,604]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressRunLifecycle.ts"},{"blob":"e5bf59fd9a26d375c91b58cffd5f7944b9c22d35","intervals":[[1,78]],"path":"src/ops/review/internal/localReview.ts"}],"job_id":"c199a92a258664412fab770657466206fa65833b652e6a1f003bb84ee7ac2e4f:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"f41687b38c35b5def763d935ec2b071ebba08574","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressEvidence.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"adbac9f6189b09c3e3713da8052822e48ab5e227","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressFileIdentity.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"cdffef4988b23df03fcc18008e63409e025604b7","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressOwnership.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"3ce4c1e2b433f255d96512bfac9ba5e745656a05","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/addressRunLifecycle.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"},{"baseline":{"method":"projection","reason":"path cluster"},"blob":"e5bf59fd9a26d375c91b58cffd5f7944b9c22d35","disposition":"included","mode":"100644","path":"src/ops/review/internal/localReview.ts","reason":"bounded verified input"}],"policy_digest":"eacd1bcf42a0e72eca72fcf9c1e9c8f97e7c515cd67a8fa7965c966924647693","repo":"camerontaylor/cq-toolkit","requested_scope":[{"blob":"f41687b